WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.983
Phobos, and Deimos.

00:02.683 --> 00:05.968
Mars has two small moons shaped like potatoes.

00:06.418 --> 00:13.331
This is Phobos, about twenty-two kilometres across, so close in that it goes round three times a day.

00:13.781 --> 00:16.762
Deimos is half the size and further out.

00:17.212 --> 00:23.126
Phobos is slowly falling: in some fifty million years it will break up, or hit Mars.
